 $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $4\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $4\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286773 1113 #uuid "f6441de6-8de3-5bac-a175-59bb496af580" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286773 1145 "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/assets/2c8a118f8f3c3ccba67e25ae09096ef1ec0cf15fc6a5e7f9de68f797b7105c80.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $4\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=4\\times 4=16\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 16 \\\\  & =96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286775 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286776 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286777 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286778 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286779 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1041 "selection" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286779 13194139534408 true] [17592186286774 1110 #uuid "2782b6c1-44f8-575b-b598-fc1156d4cd48" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286775 1034 "112\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534408 true] [17592186286775 1111 #uuid "8b5d2352-e694-5358-a6b3-759f94050fbb" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286776 1034 "80\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534408 true] [17592186286776 1111 #uuid "e0596455-f908-50bf-948d-8ad3dd7b579d" 13194139534408 true] [17592186286777 1034 "64\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 131